course: dictionary
lesson: 5163
title: Irritant: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Irritant is a noun, a naming word, and it has two meanings. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «Healthy skin is like a brick wall that keeps water in and irritants out.» Here irritants are things that make skin sore, so the skin has to keep them out. If you swap in the meaning "something that annoys you", the sentence stops making sense.
explain: The second meaning is for something or someone that annoys you, like a noisy neighbour. Ask yourself: is the word about skin, eyes, nose or throat, or about how someone feels? The answer tells you which meaning to use.
fact: An irritant is a noun: an irritant, irritants.
fact: Meaning 1: a substance that makes your skin, eyes, nose or throat sore, red or itchy.
fact: Meaning 2: something or someone that annoys you.
fact: In «irritants out», the word means things that make skin sore.
fact: Warning signs on cleaning products say "irritant", so read them carefully.
exercise: «Healthy skin keeps irritants out.» What does irritant mean here? | A soft, warm towel | A kind of healthy food | A type of wall for a garden | *Something that makes skin sore, red or itchy
exercise: On a bottle, "eye irritant" is written. What does it tell you? | *A substance that can make your eyes sore or red | A bottle that is empty | A drink that makes your eyes shine | A gift for your eyes
exercise: Ella says her neighbour's loud music is an irritant. What does she mean? | It helps her to sleep | It makes her skin sore | It is a cleaning product | *It annoys her
test: In eczema the skin «dries, cracks and lets irritants in.» What does irritants mean here? | *Things that make skin sore | Things that make skin shiny | Things that make skin smell nice | Things that keep skin dry
test: Which sentence uses irritant to mean something that annoys you? | Pollen is an eye irritant | *Her humming while I read is a real irritant | The bleach is a skin irritant | Dust is an irritant for the nose
exam: Which two meanings does irritant have? | A type of animal and a type of food | *Something that makes skin sore, and something that annoys you | Something that is always cold and something that is always wet | A kind of fruit and a kind of tool
